        lesson(
            "n4.7.1", "〜られる (passive)", "is done (by someone)",
            form: "Passive verb (食べられる, 書かれる, される, こられる); doer + に (によって for creators, discoverers and formal writing)",
            note: "The passive puts the person or thing on the receiving end first: 私は先生にほめられた (I was praised by my teacher). The doer takes に — never で or が. For something created, discovered or organized, use によって: この小説は村上春樹によって書かれた; with no doer you just leave it out (この寺は400年前に建てられた). When the thing affected belongs to you, Japanese keeps you as the subject: 私は先生に作文をほめられた. る-verb passives look like the potential (見られる = can see / is seen), so the particles tell you which one it is.",
            examples: [("小さいころ、よく母にしかられた。", "I often got scolded by my mother when I was little."), ("この橋は百年前に建てられました。", "This bridge was built a hundred years ago."), ("この曲は世界中の人に愛されている。", "This song is loved by people all over the world.")],
            keywords: ["passive", "受身", "られる", "によって"],
